WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.190
Off Sumatra, in 2004, a
magnitude 9.1 earthquake strikes.

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.130
Its toll did not stay near Sumatra.

3
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.810
People died in 10 countries
around the Indian Ocean.

4
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.250
Not one country, or two, but ten.

5
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.690
How could a single earthquake kill
people in so many different countries?

6
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.850
In this mission, you'll pin
down where an earthquake starts,

7
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.370
and why its depth matters.

8
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.210
Then you'll time seismic waves, and see
how shaking can make waterlogged ground

9
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.030
lose its strength.

10
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:38.110
Your mission: explain how one earthquake
led to deaths in 10 countries around

11
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.240
the Indian Ocean.
